From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: glacier <hyouga.dev@gmail.com>
Date: Mon, 12 Oct 2026 10:50:01 +0900
Subject: [PATCH] Stop re-testing static decorations every tick

A Survival Games map holds hundreds of item frames and paintings (Lobby_Games:
461 frames and 24 paintings inside the play area, 394 of the frames in the four
chunks around its spawn), and every tick each of them went through the
activation range once per player within 32 blocks, a chunk lookup or two in
the entity loop, and the whole of the tracker update. perf on the VPS put those
paths at about 9% of a 20-player server's CPU.

- ActivationRange: a chunk with no monster or animal (counted per chunk at
  Chunk.addEntity/removeEntityAtIndex, checked by the index audit) has only
  misc entities to activate, and they are reached through the slice's X/Z
  bucket index, only the buckets the misc box can reach. Always-active
  entities are no longer stamped there; their activatedTick is never read.
- checkIfActive looks the chunk up only for an active entity, and the inactive
  path asks the entity's type before the chunk.
- EntityTrackerEntry: a hanging entity with no viewer that has not moved or
  changed only advances its counter, which is all the full update did; an item
  frame reads its item only on the ticks that use it.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>

